==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|ballista||a military siege engine for throwing stones}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bəˈlɪst.ɪk/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{label|en|not comparable}} Or relating to [[ballistics]].
# {{label|en|comparable}} Or relating to [[projectile]]s moving under their own [[momentum]], air drag, [[gravity]] and sometimes [[rocket]] power
# {{label|en|comparable|slang}} Very [[angry]].
#: ''When he heard him lie about it, he went '''ballistic'''.''

